From 2f5c64772434907e11c838af021bcfb120631a18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 10:16:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Couch Party / LAN: use the stock VS / Battle results menu
 after a race

After a Couch Party or LAN GAME race the results were an overlay panel.
They are now the game's own VS / Battle results menu, the same one a
2-4 player VS race shows: the fade to black, the VS or BATTLE title, the
character portraits with win counts and the winner's celebration, and
Retry / Course change / Driver change / Quit with the stock cursor,
sounds and fade.

- 2-4 players: the stock portraits, with the couch party's own wins and
  1st/2nd/3rd counts for this session.
- 5-8 players: the four portraits don't fit, so the same menu lists every
  player's place, number, driver and wins in the game's font.
- Players 5-8 can work the menu too (they're added to the combined
  controller while the results are up).
- The menu's own fade-in and portrait slide take about 1.5 seconds before
  it reads input, and it only reacts to new presses, so buttons from the
  end of the race still can't pick an option.
- The menu runs and is drawn once over the whole window, not inside each
  player's view.
- The winner's view isn't zoomed to full screen first: every player keeps
  their own view behind the menu.
